===Alternative forms===
* [[veugel]] (obsolete)

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|odt|nl}} {{term|fogal|lang=odt}}, {{term|vogal|lang=odt}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|nl}} {{recons|fuglaz|lang=gem-pro}}. Cognate with Low German {{term|Vagel|lang=nds}}, German {{term|Vogel|lang=de}}, West Frisian {{term|fûgel|lang=fy}}, English ''[[fowl]]'', Danish {{term|fugl|lang=da}}, Swedish ''[[fågel]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Nl-vogel.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|m|vogels|pl2=vogelen|vogeltje}}

# A [[bird]], feathered animal
# A [[gaai]], a [[feathered]] target in [[archery]] or [[shooting]]
# {{figuratively}} A [[dude]]

